Chromium isn't installed for playwright. Installing a browser may not be possible offline. Let me not rely on that. The syntax check passed and the file serves with HTTP 200. That's sufficient verification for a single-file HTML game. I could do a more thorough runtime sanity check using Node with a DOM shim, but that's overkill and jsdom isn't available likely.

Let me do a final review of the game logic for any obvious bugs:

1. `game.startGame` → `setupPlayers` → `assignRoles` → `placeTasks`, then cinematic. Good.
2. During cinematic, state==='CINEMATIC', loop moves players rightward. When cinematicEnd reached, `beginCinematicPhase2` called. It sets another cinematicEnd and after 4s calls revealRoles → state PLAYING. Good.
3. In revealRoles, sets action buttons HTML. Good.
4. In PLAYING, local player updates from input in loop (I duplicated movement in loop AND in Player.update for local). Actually Player.update for local id reads input and applies movement, and then loop ALSO applies movement for local player when !vent. Double movement! Let me check: In Player.update, if id===localId, it computes ax,ay and updates this.x/this.y with collision. Then in loop, again: `if(players[localId] && ... state==='PLAYING'){ ... p.x=nx... }`. So local player moves twice per frame → 2x speed but still functional. Not a bug that breaks playability, but let me fix to avoid double. Actually Player.update handles local input movement; loop's extra block duplicates it. Let me remove the duplicate in loop to keep single source. But Player.update also handles bots. So I should make Player.update handle movement for all (local input + bot AI), and remove the loop duplication. Let me edit.

Also in Player.update for local, after computing nx,ny with collision it sets this.x=nx,this.y=ny. Then loop overrides again. Fine functionally but double speed. Let me clean: remove the local-movement block in loop, keep Player.update as the single mover.

But wait: Player.update for local reads `input` global — good. And loop calls p.update(dt) for all players. So just remove the loop block. Let me edit.

2. `setLayers([])` clears all layers — used when entering PLAYING. Good. But the roletext is a separate div not in .layer, controlled by display. Good.

3. `updateActions` sets innerHTML of #actions. Good.

4. Task sub-UI: `pollTaskInit` uses `game.taskTarget` — fine.

5. In `endMeeting`, judge logic: if judgeMark===ejected and isImp → marked dies. Else if ejected set → ejected dies. Good. But when judge marks and isImp correct, it says "era un impostor" and marked dies. When wrong, "no era impostor. El juez es expulsado" and local dies. Matches spec roughly.

6. Win conditions implemented. Good.

7. Bodies: snake dissolve, report. Good.

Let me fix the double movement by editing the loop block. Let me also make sure `this.beginCinematicPhase2 ? ...` is cleaned. I'll edit loop.

Let me do the edit to remove duplicate local movement in loop.

Current loop section:
```
  // input motion
  if(players[localId] && players[localId].alive && state==='PLAYING'){
    const p = players[localId];
    if(!p.vent){
      let ax=(input.right-input.left)*150, ay=(input.down-input.up)*150;
      if(input.touch.active){ ax += input.touch.dx*150; ay += input.touch.dy*150; }
      const m = Math.hypot(ax,ay);
      if(m>150){ ax*=150/m; ay*=150/m; }
      let nx=p.x+ax*dt, ny=p.y+ay*dt;
      for(const w of WALLS){ const s=rectCollide({x:nx,y:ny,r:p.r}, w); nx+=s.x; ny+=s.y; }
      nx=clamp(nx,p.r+20,WORLD.w-p.r-20); ny=clamp(ny,p.r+20,WORLD.h-p.r-20);
      p.x=nx; p.y=ny;
      if(m>5) p.angle = Math.atan2(ay,ax);
    }
  }
  // update entities
  for(const p of players) p.update(dt);
```

I'll remove the first block since Player.update handles it. Let me edit.

Also, in Player.update local movement, the vent check: if p.vent, vx=vy=0 return — good (can't move in vent).

Let me apply edit.

